  <main_text>
    <l n="1">amore, exercetur, illius defen-</l>
    <l n="2">dendi gratia, majorisque mali</l>
    <l n="3">&amp; quidem imminentis aver-</l>
    <l n="4">tendi. In tantum etiam, ut</l>
    <l n="5">dulce ac decorum habeatur pro</l>
    <l n="6">Patriæ salute &amp; incolumitate</l>
    <l n="7">mortis periculum intrepidè</l>
    <l n="8">subire; cui dulcissimę vitam &amp;</l>
    <l n="9">omnia jure debemus. Ut sin-</l>
    <l n="10">gulare certamen in Patriæ</l>
    <l n="11">commoduṁ[?] atque emolu-</l>
    <l n="12">mentum suscepţum[?], sublimi-</l>
    <l n="13">tatione postmodum explican-</l>
    <l n="14">dā, non tantum licitum sit, ve-</l>
    <l n="15">rùm insuper gloriosum. Tale</l>
    <l n="16">fuit certamen Manlii Torqua-</l>
    <l n="17">ti, ita appellati, à devicto ho-</l>
    <l n="18">ste Gallo, cui torquem detra-</l>
    <l n="19">xerat.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">Horatiorum ac Curiatiorum</l>
    <l n="21">fratrum inter Romanos &amp; Al-</l>
    <l n="22">banos, super jure superiorita-</l>
    <l n="23">tis ac dominii.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">Et suadeṭ[?] hoc genus certa-</l>
    <l n="25">minis instinctus ac ratio naturæ,</l>
    <l n="26">secundum quam unum-</l>
  </main_text>
